cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenVideoHarness in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenVideoHarness: A Code-to-Video Harness for Coding Agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ZLHad and contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZLHad/OpenVideoHarness"
url: "https://github.com/ZLHad/OpenVideoHarness"
license: MIT
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
abstract: >-
  A video-as-code harness that turns coding agents such as Claude Code and Codex into a multi-genre video studio:
  every frame is a pure function of time, the agent reviews its own rendered frames, and people approve the concept
  and the first draft, and the storyboard of a costly film. It ships 11 video types (two experimental), 33 style presets with rendered swatches, and code-composed
  music, voice, captions, mixing and audio QA.
keywords:
  - video-as-code
  - code2video
  - coding-agents
  - motion-graphics
  - text-to-speech
  - hyperframes
  - manim
